training and evaluation children -- which execute different modules and therefore have
different closures -- are each required to be consistent among themselves instead of
being required to be identical to one another. `check_arm_identities` then compares what
really ran with the approved `code.haa_finetune` / `code.haa_eval` and each room's
approved `artifacts.heading` digest. `arm_headings` requires one heading record per room
across every seed of the arm, and `child_protocol` / `check_test_indices` re-apply
exp_02's frozen protocol (K = 8, eval_seed 0, split test, the DiffRIR indices in order).

